 //    ]
 ```
 
+##### limit
+
+The maximum number of ranges to return, defaults to unlimited. When the header
+contains more valid ranges than `limit` (counted after `combine`, if enabled),
+they are coalesced into a single range from the lowest start to the highest end,
+rather than being truncated or rejected. This lets a response be served (and
+cached) as a single range instead of multipart.
+
+<!-- eslint-disable no-undef -->
+
+```js
+parseRange(100, 'bytes=0-10,50-60,80-90', { limit: 2 })
+// => [{ start: 0, end: 90 }]
+```
+
